Input: {"question": "What is the length of the New England 200 race?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0463-22f0bb61fa30:d00", "start": 0, "end": 132, "text": "Lakes Region 200 The Lakes Region 200 is a NASCAR Xfinity Series race held at New Hampshire Motor Speedway in Loudon, New Hampshire."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0463-22f0bb61fa30:d00", "start": 133, "end": 180, "text": "When first held in 1990, the race was 300 laps."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0463-22f0bb61fa30:d00", "start": 181, "end": 314, "text": "It was scaled back to 250 laps, the length of the former fall NHMS race, starting in 1993, and again to its current 200 laps in 1996."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0463-22f0bb61fa30:d00", "start": 315, "end": 483, "text": "Until 2010, in twenty three races held at NHMS, there had never been a repeat Xfinity Series winner, the longest such streak in any of NASCAR's national touring series."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0463-22f0bb61fa30:d00", "start": 484, "end": 544, "text": "Kyle Busch broke the streak with victories in 2009 and 2010."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0463-22f0bb61fa30:d01", "start": 0, "end": 115, "text": "The Lakes Region 200 is a NASCAR Xfinity Series race held at New Hampshire Motor Speedway in Loudon, New Hampshire."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0463-22f0bb61fa30:d01", "start": 116, "end": 163, "text": "When first held in 1990, the race was 300 laps."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0463-22f0bb61fa30:d01", "start": 164, "end": 305, "text": "It was scaled back to 250 laps, the length of the former fall NHMS race, starting in 1993, and then expanded to its current 500 laps in 1996."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0463-22f0bb61fa30:d01", "start": 306, "end": 474, "text": "Until 2010, in twenty three races held at NHMS, there had